<section class="lsec rv " id="why" aria-labelledby="h-why"><!-- DYNAMIC: $landing->sections[0] (split) -->
 <div class="lw"><p class="eyb"><span>01 · Why dedicated</span></p><h2 id="h-why">Why Hire a Dedicated Senior Developer Instead of a Platform Freelancer</h2><div class="split"><div><p class=lead>Fiverr and Upwork have thousands of developers listed from Karachi and across Pakistan; most are task-takers, not system thinkers. When you need a custom CRM that handles 1,000+ leads per day, a multi-tenant SaaS platform your clients pay monthly for, or an automation system that replaces five manual processes, you are not buying a gig. You are making an architectural decision that will shape your operations for the next three to five years.</p><p>I have shipped multi-tenant CRMs with 300+ concurrent users, payroll systems that process monthly cycles reliably, and enterprise ticketing portals that replaced email-chain chaos with auditable workflows. The difference shows in systems that still run cleanly twelve months after handover, not in the per-hour rate on a profile page.</p></div>
 <aside class="wbox"><small>Full project ownership</small><ul class="pills"><li>Requirements analysis</li><li>Database architecture</li><li>Weekly demos</li><li>Production deployment</li><li>Team documentation</li><li>Post-launch support</li></ul><p>A fundamentally different engagement than commissioning a task on a marketplace.</p></aside></div></div>
</section>

<section class="lsec rv dark" id="signs" aria-labelledby="h-signs"><!-- DYNAMIC: $landing->sections[1] (signs) -->
 <div class="lw"><p class="eyb"><span>02 · Signs</span></p><h2 id="h-signs">Signs Your Business Needs a Custom Software Developer</h2><p class="lead nar">Most businesses reach the same breaking point at different speeds. If any of these sound familiar, off-the-shelf tools have hit their ceiling:</p>
 <div class="sit s3"><div><span class="nn">01</span><p>Your team manages leads, orders or operations in spreadsheets that break under volume.</p></div><div><span class="nn">02</span><p>You pay per-seat licensing fees on a CRM that doesn’t match your actual sales process.</p></div><div><span class="nn">03</span><p>Your developers spend more time working around your platform than building on it.</p></div><div><span class="nn">04</span><p>Data is siloed across three or four tools with no single source of truth.</p></div><div><span class="nn">05</span><p>Onboarding a new client or branch means manually replicating configurations.</p></div><div><span class="nn">06</span><p>Reporting needs someone to export, merge and clean data every time management needs a number.</p></div></div>
 <div class="rep wide"><b>The fix</b><p>Custom software built by a senior developer in Karachi addresses these at the architecture level, not with another tool on top: a system your team runs without a developer ticket for every report, that scales without a full rebuild when user counts double.</p></div>
